pod_engi.guide.main.title=Machines Add-On
pod_engi.guide.main.body=§o§7by Podcrash§r%1%1Welcome to the Machines Add-On, which adds a bunch of new machines, items, and blocks to your game!%1%1This book will introduce you to all the machines, items, and crafting recipes this Add-On adds to the game. If you ever lose this book, you can simply craft it again with a book and a piece of §mredstone§r.%1%1For more detailed information, check out §3§ohttps://pdcr.sh/machines§r%1%1Reach out to §3§ohelp.podcrash.com§r if you've found an issue!
pod_engi.guide.how_to_machines.title=How to Interact with Machines
pod_engi.guide.how_to_machines.body=There are 3 types of ports to be aware of when connecting pipes to machines:%1%1§l§bLiquid ports§r%1These ports are used to transfer liquid in/out of a machine using Glass Pipes.%1%1§l§6Power ports§r%1These ports are used to power machines with Copper Pipes.%1%1§l§7Item ports§r%1These ports are used to transfer items in/out of machines with Iron Pipes.%1%1Generally, an input port will be coloured §9blue§r and an output port will be coloured §cred§r.%1%1Some machines can be interacted with to see more information about their internal states. %1%1The Steam Engine, for example, can be interacted with to see how much coal, water, and power is stored inside.%1%1Pipes will be oriented depending on which block you placed them against. They'll almost always automatically make the connections you want, but if they don't, simply use a wrench on the side of a pipe you want to change, and it will split off in that direction. You can remove a pipe connection by interacting again.
pod_engi.guide.generators.title=Generators
pod_engi.guide.generators.body=These machines will produce power for you, typically by converting other resources into it.
pod_engi.guide.steam_engine.title=Steam Engine
pod_engi.guide.steam_engine.body=The most basic generator you can make, and an important priority for the early game. It only works with a steady supply of coal and water, so make sure to connect it to a pump as well. To help the generator get started once it's connected to the pump, you'll have to interact with it with a bucket of water. After that, the generator will power the pump and supply water to itself!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%12 3 2%11 4 1%1%11 = Sturdy Frame%12 = Redstone Dust%13 = Blast Furnace%14 = Block of Copper%1%1Crafts 1 Steam Engine.
pod_engi.guide.bio_reactor.title=Bio-reactor
pod_engi.guide.bio_reactor.body=A very flexible generator, which will give different amounts of power depending on what kind of bio-fuel you put into it.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%15 6 5%1%11 = Copper Wire%12 = Composter%13 = Logic Circuit%14 = Smoker%15 = Sturdy Frame%16 = Iron Gear%1%1Crafts 1 Bio-reactor.
pod_engi.guide.thermal_generator.title=Thermal Generator
pod_engi.guide.thermal_generator.body=An upgrade from the steam engine which not only gives more power, but will be useful in places where water is hard to come by, like the Nether!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%15 6 5%1%11 = Iron Gear%12 = Logic Circuit%13 = Steam Engine%14 = Ignition Powder%15 = Sturdy Frame%16 = Cauldron%1%1Crafts 1 Thermal Generator.
pod_engi.guide.solar_engine.title=Solar Engine
pod_engi.guide.solar_engine.body=A late game generator that will work anytime there is sunlight, freely supplying power with no extra input on your part! It's hard to craft, but is worth the effort!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%1§0X X X§r%11 2 1%13 4 3%1%11 = Refined Metal Ingot%12 = Daylight Detector%13 = Null Copper Block%14 = Calibrated Circuit%1%1Crafts 1 Solar Engine.
pod_engi.guide.machines.title=Machines
pod_engi.guide.machines.body=There are many different machines to create in this Add-On. %1%1Some machines will allow you to produce new resources, others offer utility, and some are just for fun!
pod_engi.guide.gear_stamper.title=Gear Stamper
pod_engi.guide.gear_stamper.body=A simple machine that takes an input of iron ingots and power and stamps them into iron gears, an important resource for later recipes.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%11 5 1%1%11 = Sturdy Frame%12 = Piston%13 = Refined Metal Ingot%14 = Refined Metal Block%15 = Copper Ingot%1%1Crafts 1 Gear Stamper.
pod_engi.guide.wire_extruder.title=Wire Extruder
pod_engi.guide.wire_extruder.body=A simple machine that takes an input of copper ingots and power and outputs copper wire, a useful resource for later recipes.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%12 3 2%11 2 1%1%11 = Sturdy Frame%12 = Iron Gear%13 = Loom%1%1Crafts 1 Wire Extruder.
pod_engi.guide.item_depositor.title=Item Depositor
pod_engi.guide.item_depositor.body=A basic device, which grabs the top of a storage container that it's placed on top of and deposits whatever items are coming to it from an Iron Item Pipe into the container.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%11 2 1%1%11 = Refined Metal Ingot%12 = Iron Item Pipe%13 = Redstone Dust%14 = Dropper%1%1Crafts 1 Item Depositor.
pod_engi.guide.item_extractor.title=Item Extractor
pod_engi.guide.item_extractor.body=A basic device, with grabs hold of a storage container and sends what items are inside through connected Iron Item Pipes. The extractor will only take what is needed, so don't worry about misplacing your treasured pickaxe in your fuel chest and watching it burn!%1%1If it's connected to an Item Depositor, it'll move everything from the connected container to the depositor, in case you want to move loads of items passively and create a storage system!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%11 2 1%1%11 = Refined Metal Ingot%12 = Iron Item Pipe%13 = Copper Ingot%14 = Hopper%1%1Crafts 1 Item Extractor.
pod_engi.guide.pump.title=Pump
pod_engi.guide.pump.body=Place it above water or lava and supply it with power, and the pump will supply any machines that need it!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%1§0X§r 1 §0X§r%12 3 2%14 5 4%1%11 = Iron Item Pipe%12 = Copper Ingot%13 = Glass%14 = Refined Metal Block%15 = Sturdy Frame%1%1Crafts 1 Pump.
pod_engi.guide.guster.title=Guster
pod_engi.guide.guster.body=The most flexible and fun device a new machinist can make. When supplied with power, the Guster will launch whatever is in front of it with immense force. You can launch yourself, mobs, and even projectiles such as lit TNT to create a long-range cannon! There's lots of great uses for this, so get creative!%1%1There's a small charge time, depending on the amount of power you supply the Guster with. More power means it'll activate more often! Additionally, you can stack multiple Gusters on top of or in front of each other to massively increase their propelling force!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%11 5 1%1%11 = Sturdy Frame%12 = Ignition Powder%13 = Iron Gear%14 = Breeze Rod%15 = Logic Circuit%1%1Crafts 1 Guster.
pod_engi.guide.drill_controller.title=Drill Controller
pod_engi.guide.drill_controller.body=A machine that, when set down next to a frame of Truss blocks, will power a quarry and dig out the blocks in the frame, outputting them to the side of the controller.%1%1To make a quarry, create a complete square (with the corners filled in!) of Truss blocks outlining the area you want to dig out. The maximum boundaries are 12x12 blocks. The Drill Controller should be placed with it's back touching one of the Truss blocks in the outline, and power supplied to it's input. The quarry will then drill out all the blocks down to bedrock, and output those items for you!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%1§0X§r 1 §0X§r%12 3 2%14 5 4%1%11 = Lever%12 = Calibrated Circuit%13 = Item Extractor%14 = Refined Metal Block%15 = Lectern%1%1Crafts 1 Drill Controller.
pod_engi.guide.mob_muncher.title=Mob Muncher
pod_engi.guide.mob_muncher.body=A dangerous looking machine that harnesses the power of sculk to "munch" nearby mobs, collecting their drops and experience, or "essence". You'll need to supply it with a lot of power, but in return you'll have a way to passively grind mobs!%1You can also connect a glass liquid pipe to it and move the essence to the lightning rod calibrator.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%11 3 1%14 5 4%1%11 = Null Copper Ingot%12 = Sculk Sensor%13 = Calibrated Circuit%14 = Sturdy Frame%15 = Sculk Catalyst%1%1Crafts 1 Mob Muncher.
pod_engi.guide.lightning_rod_calibrator.title=Lightning Rod Calibrator
pod_engi.guide.lightning_rod_calibrator.body=Forces the weather to become a thunderstorm! As long as the machine is steadily supplied essence from the Mob Muncher, it'll maintain the thunderstorm.%1A lightning rod must be placed on top of the Lightning Rod Calibrator in order for it to work.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%15 6 5%1%11 = Null Copper Ingot%12 = Refined Metal Block%13 = Copper Wire%14 = Calibrated Circuit%15 = Glass%16 = Sturdy Frame%1%1Crafts 1 Lightning Rod Calibrator.
pod_engi.guide.connectors.title=Connectors
pod_engi.guide.connectors.body=Connectors allow you to connect different machines to each-other, creating production lines!
pod_engi.guide.iron_item_pipe.title=Iron Item Pipe
pod_engi.guide.iron_item_pipe.body=A pipe that connects machines and transports items where they're needed.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 1 1%1§0X X X§r%11 1 1%1%11 = Iron Ingot%1%1Crafts 12 Iron Item Pipe.
pod_engi.guide.copper_power_pipe.title=Copper Power Pipe
pod_engi.guide.copper_power_pipe.body=A pipe that allows you to take power from your generators and move it to the machines that need it.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 1 1%1§0X X X§r%11 1 1%1%11 = Copper Ingot%1%1Crafts 12 Coper Power Pipe.
pod_engi.guide.glass_liquid_pipe.title=Glass Liquid Pipe
pod_engi.guide.glass_liquid_pipe.body=A pipe that lets you move water, magma, and essence around to different machines.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 1 1%1§0X X X§r%11 1 1%1%11 = Glass%1%1Crafts 12 Glass Liquid Pipe.
pod_engi.guide.items.title=Items
pod_engi.guide.items.body=Important tools and equipment for any machinist to use.
pod_engi.guide.wrench.title=Wrench
pod_engi.guide.wrench.body=The most important tool for a practicing machinist, it allows you to manipulate pipe connections to your machines!%1%1You can also use it to identify the type of port you're dealing with by looking at it.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%1§0X§r 1 §0X§r%1§0X§r 2 §0X§r%1§0X§r 2 §0X§r%1%11 = Iron Ingot%12 = Copper Ingot%1%1Crafts 1 Wrench.
pod_engi.guide.gust_pack.title=Gust Pack
pod_engi.guide.gust_pack.body=Launches you high into the air, but without any safety features to prevent fall damage, so be careful! %1%1It's best used to launch yourself up to high places or out of deep water. You can even prevent taking lethal fall damage by using it just before you hit the ground!%1%1To use the Gust Pack, you have to jump while sneaking or falling. You can only use it a few times before needing to land. Using it multiple times in a row will cause it to degrade faster.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%13 4 3%15 §0X§r 5%1%11 = Copper Wire%12 = Calibrated Circuit%13 = Ignition Powder%14 = Iron Leggings%15 = Guster%1%1Crafts 1 Gust Pack.
pod_engi.guide.hard_hat.title=Hard-Hat
pod_engi.guide.hard_hat.body=A piece of armour to show you're a machinist! Gives some moderate protection as well.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%1§0X X X§r%11 1 1%12 §0X§r 2%1%11 = Refined Metal Ingot%12 = Fabric%1%1Crafts 1 Hard-hat.
pod_engi.guide.resources.title=Resources
pod_engi.guide.resources.body=A list of all the new kinds of resources you'll be making and using in this Add-On!
pod_engi.guide.iron_coal_clump.title=Iron and Coal Clump
pod_engi.guide.iron_coal_clump.body=A messy combination of Raw Iron and Coal, ready to be refined into Refined Metal by smelting in a furnace.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%1Combine the following items in any shape:%1%13x Coal%11x Iron Ingot%1%1Crafts 1 Iron and Coal Clump.
pod_engi.guide.refined_metal.title=Refined Metal
pod_engi.guide.refined_metal.body=An ingot that is important for crafting most of the items that a machinist can make, created by smelting an Iron and Coal Clump.
pod_engi.guide.refined_metal_block.title=Refined Metal Block
pod_engi.guide.refined_metal_block.body=9 Refined Metal combined into a single block for decoration or crafting.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 1 1%11 1 1%11 1 1%1%11 = Iron Ingot%1%1Crafts 1 Refined Metal Block.
pod_engi.guide.raw_null_copper.title=Raw Null Copper
pod_engi.guide.raw_null_copper.body=An unstable fusion of Ender Pearls and Copper, which must be stabilized by heat in a furnace in order to create Null Copper Ingot.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%1Combine the following items in any shape:%1%13x Ender Pearl%11x Raw Copper%1%1Crafts 1 Raw Null Copper.
pod_engi.guide.null_copper.title=Null Copper Ingot
pod_engi.guide.null_copper.body=An otherworldly ingot required for some of the most advanced machines a machinist can make.%1Created by smelting Raw Null Copper.
pod_engi.guide.null_copper_block.title=Null Copper Block
pod_engi.guide.null_copper_block.body=9 Null Copper Ingots combined into a single block for decoration or crafting.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 1 1%11 1 1%11 1 1%1%11 = Null Copper Ingot%1%1Crafts 1 Null Copper Block.
pod_engi.guide.fabric.title=Fabric
pod_engi.guide.fabric.body=Woven from string and used for the Hard-Hat!%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 1 §0X§r%11 1 §0X§r%11 1 §0X§r%1%11 = String%1%1Crafts 3 Fabric.
pod_engi.guide.truss.title=Truss
pod_engi.guide.truss.body=Metal scaffolding, which can be used for decoration or, most importantly, to create your own quarry with the Drill Controller.%1%1A platform variant of the Truss can be crafted in a similar manner to slabs.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%12 §0X§r 2%11 2 1%1%11 = Refined Metal Ingot%12 = Stick%1%1Crafts 16 Truss.
pod_engi.guide.sturdy_frame.title=Sturdy Frame
pod_engi.guide.sturdy_frame.body=Refined Metal combined with wood into a strong frame. An important block used in crafting most machines.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 1%12 §0X§r 2%11 2 1%1%11 = Refined Metal Ingot%12 = Planks%1%1Crafts 1 Sturdy Frame.
pod_engi.guide.ignition_powder.title=Ignition Powder
pod_engi.guide.ignition_powder.body=An extremely dangerous combination of gunpowder, wind charges, and blaze powder. A required reagent in propulsion machines, like the Guster.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 3%11 2 3%11 2 3%1%11 = Blaze Powder%12 = Gunpowder%13 = Wind Charge%1%1Crafts 1 Ignition Powder.
pod_engi.guide.logic_circuit.title=Logic Circuit
pod_engi.guide.logic_circuit.body=A delicately hand-made circuit, used in crafting machines with some complexity.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 3%12 4 §0X§r%11 3 §0X§r%1%11 = Refined Metal Ingot%12 = Redstone Dust%13 = Copper Wire%14 = Nether Quartz%1%1Crafts 1 Logic Circuit.
pod_engi.guide.calibrated_circuit.title=Calibrated Circuit
pod_engi.guide.calibrated_circuit.body=An upgrade to the Logic Circuit used in the most complicated machines.%1%1§lCrafting§r%1%11 2 3%12 4 §0X§r%11 3 §0X§r%1%11 = Null Copper Ingot%12 = Amethyst Shard%13 = Gold Ingot%14 = Logic Circuit%1%1Crafts 1 Calibrated Circuit.
pod_engi.guide.copper_wire.title=Copper Wire
pod_engi.guide.copper_wire.body=A crafting ingredient created by the Wire Extruder.%1%1§lIngredients§r %11x Copper
pod_engi.guide.iron_gear.title=Iron Gear
pod_engi.guide.iron_gear.body=A crafting ingredient created by the Gear Stamper.%1%1§lIngredients§r %11x Iron
